{
  "opportunity_id": "proc_29870ead40",
  "source": "content_cluster",
  "title": "Extending deals in Sitara/Unify to cover gas that already flowed",
  "task_class": "deal_entry_correction",
  "label_mechanical": "Deal entry and correction in Sitara / Unify / TAGG: extend cover / deal / flowed",
  "narrative": {
    "what_happens": "Someone reviewing meter activity finds volume that flowed on days with no matching deal, or a deal whose term ends before the gas stopped moving. They mail the deal owner or scheduler with the meter number, the specific dates and decatherm quantities, and ask that the existing deal be extended to cover the gap so downstream accounting can be built against it. In some cases the request is forward-looking (\"extend the deal to cover September\"), in others it is retroactive and the flow dates are months or more than a year old. The thread ends when the deal is stretched over the missing period; where the history is old, the exchange turns into a back-and-forth about why the gap was only just discovered and which desk or system was live at the time.",
    "where_it_stalls": "Every message in this cluster carries a rework signal: the deal record is being corrected after the fact rather than captured correctly at entry. The stall is discovery latency \u2014 unlinked flow sits at a meter until someone happens to reconcile it, and by then the parties have to reconstruct context (\"Is this date really June of 1999?\", \"The East Desk was not up and running on Unify in June of 1999\"). Requests are also one-directional: the requester supplies dates and volumes but cannot make the change themselves, and at least one thread shows waiting on the other party before Volume Management can create the accounting arrangement.",
    "why_it_recurs": "Gas flows at a meter whether or not a deal covers the term, and nothing forces the deal end-date to match actual flow, so each reconciliation pass turns up a fresh set of uncovered days needing a manual extension request.",
    "automation_opportunity": "A scheduled exception report that joins measured meter volumes against deal terms and lists days with flow but no covering deal, mailed to the deal owner with meter, dates and quantities pre-filled \u2014 turning the ad-hoc discovery mail into a standing worklist, ideally with a one-click deal-extension request rather than free-text email.",
    "coherence": "tight"
  },
